From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:18:50 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] Plutonium: native windows, terminals and browser tabs
 in a thread's right panel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Folded from:
- list agent-launched native windows under their thread
- apps in the right panel, terminal tagging, pop out
- use the Plutonium helper and its agent bridge
- panel tab keys, new browser tab, app launcher
- thread tags, groups and the Elsewhere list
- import browser tabs from other shells into a thread
- links and Ctrl+click open in the thread's browser panel
- panel apps cross-fade on resize, and their maximize button maximizes the panel
- the server drives the browser panel's tabs through Plutonium's helper
- what the user starts comes to the front; a toast for the rest
- windows held at an agent's size, Take control; read_window and act_window
- several displays: a placeholder for a window another display took, To display N
- agent tool fixes: popups in window snapshots, results that say what happened, private tabs marked
- the dock: Super+1…9 slots for the terminal, apps and sites
- the dock in the sidebar, above the settings row
- dock sites kept per project or everywhere
- remote clients see native windows
- a link opened in a new tab shows in the browser panel
- the status cluster: clock, battery and quick settings in the title bar
- a dock slot holds one window or tab
- dock sites' icons from the helper
- an agent's hidden tabs get a panel tab, added in the background
